WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.278 --> 00:00:01.696
- Hi, I'm Nick Ortiz.

00:00:01.696 --> 00:00:04.662
I'm a board certified
disability insurance attorney.

00:00:04.662 --> 00:00:05.859
Today I'm here to talk to you about

00:00:05.859 --> 00:00:07.973
Prudential Life Insurance Company.

00:00:07.973 --> 00:00:09.980
Also known as Prudential Financial,

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:11.674
or Prudential for short.

00:00:11.674 --> 00:00:13.086
You're probably here because Prudential

00:00:13.086 --> 00:00:15.476
has denied or terminated your benefits

00:00:15.476 --> 00:00:18.846
for long term disability
insurance benefits.

00:00:18.846 --> 00:00:21.053
Or, LTD benefits for short.

00:00:21.053 --> 00:00:22.777
There are several reasons why Prudential

00:00:22.777 --> 00:00:24.279
may have denied your claim.

00:00:24.279 --> 00:00:26.891
Perhaps the most common is
that they've sent your file

00:00:26.891 --> 00:00:28.870
to one of their doctors for a review,

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:30.907
and their doctor basically has concluded

00:00:30.907 --> 00:00:32.930
that you can go back to work.

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:35.001
A second reason why they might
have denied your claim is

00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:36.851
because they've had your file reviewed

00:00:36.851 --> 00:00:40.225
by a vocational expert or a job expert.

00:00:40.225 --> 00:00:42.488
And that job expert has concluded

00:00:42.488 --> 00:00:45.434
that given the restrictions that they see

00:00:45.434 --> 00:00:48.467
in your medical record, or
as defined by their doctor

00:00:48.467 --> 00:00:50.527
that you can go back to work.

00:00:50.527 --> 00:00:52.411
A third reason why Prudential
may have denied your claim

00:00:52.411 --> 00:00:53.948
is because of a change in the

00:00:53.948 --> 00:00:56.125
definition of the term disability.

00:00:56.125 --> 00:00:58.849
What that means is, that
for the first two years

00:00:58.849 --> 00:01:01.421
of your policy they may
pay benefits so long as you

00:01:01.421 --> 00:01:04.105
cannot perform the material
duties of your job.

00:01:04.105 --> 00:01:07.394
That is your occupation,
your own occupation

00:01:07.394 --> 00:01:10.133
or what we call own occ for short.

00:01:10.133 --> 00:01:12.860
But after two years, they
typically will broaden

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:16.150
that definition to see
whether you can do any job

00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:18.117
or any occupation.

00:01:18.117 --> 00:01:19.690
And while Prudential
may have agreed that you

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:22.180
could not perform your own occupation,

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:24.360
they may feel that you can do other work

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:28.283
or any occupation and deny your
case at that two year mark.

00:01:28.283 --> 00:01:29.911
Fourth reason why Prudential
might deny your claim

00:01:29.911 --> 00:01:32.672
is they say that there's
insufficient medical evidence

00:01:32.672 --> 00:01:33.787
to support the claim.

00:01:33.787 --> 00:01:34.891
What that may mean is,

00:01:34.891 --> 00:01:36.532
you stopped going to the doctors,

00:01:36.532 --> 00:01:39.508
so there's no new medical
evidence to support the case.

00:01:39.508 --> 00:01:42.198
Or there's been some
improvement in your condition

00:01:42.198 --> 00:01:44.595
through the healing process
and they think that based on

00:01:44.595 --> 00:01:47.619
that improvement you
could go back to work.

00:01:47.619 --> 00:01:49.713
So those are some of the basic reasons

00:01:49.713 --> 00:01:51.680
why Prudential denies claims.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:53.988
But the good news is, that you
do have the right to appeal

00:01:53.988 --> 00:01:58.358
their either denial of benefits,
or termination of benefits.

00:01:58.358 --> 00:02:00.278
And that's where talking to an experienced

00:02:00.278 --> 00:02:02.369
long term disability attorney can help.

00:02:02.369 --> 00:02:04.782
I personally have experience
in handling claims

00:02:04.782 --> 00:02:07.732
against Prudential and long
term disability insurance claims

00:02:07.732 --> 00:02:10.130
and we welcome an
opportunity to speak to you

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:12.354
